WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Making a Schedule of Loss can take time. You need to check contracts, payslips and other case files.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.000
With Lylo, you add the case files and Lylo starts to build the draft.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:21.500
It pulls out key facts and adds the losses into one clear Schedule of Loss.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.000
Open Citations to see where each key figure came from, down to the file and page.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Calculations shows how each total was worked out, so you can check the maths.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:46.000
If Lylo is not sure about something, it tells you. It marks it for review, so you can check it and make the final call.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:58.000
You can edit the draft yourself, just like a normal document. Or, tell Lylo what you want changed in chat, and Lylo can update it for you.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.500
You can also add more types of loss, like notice pay, holiday pay, benefits and interest.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:15.500
In the end, you get one clear draft with the facts, maths and points to check all in one place.
